    "markdown": "---\ntitle: load\n---\n\n\n\n```python\nload(\n    dataset,\n    scale=None,\n    years=None,\n    variables=None,\n    wide=None,\n    geometry=False,\n    names=False,\n    groups=None,\n    ref=None,\n)\n```\n\nLoad a dataset as a panel: one row per unit (``geo_id``) and year.\n\n## Parameters {.doc-section .doc-section-parameters}\n\n| Name      | Type        | Description                                                                                                                            | Default    |\n|-----------|-------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|\n| dataset   | str         | Dataset id (see ``geo.datasets()``)                                                                                                    | _required_ |\n| scale     | str \\| None | Scale to load; defaults to the dataset's native scale                                                                                  | `None`     |\n| years     |             | An int, a list of ints, or a ``(first, last)`` range (inclusive)                                                                       | `None`     |\n| variables |             | A variable or list of variables to keep (``geo_id`` and ``year`` are always kept); ``geo.search()`` and ``geo.dictionary()`` list them | `None`     |\n| wide      | str \\| None | A variable name; returns one row per unit with one column per year (``<variable><year>``)                                              | `None`     |\n| geometry  | bool        | Attach unit boundaries (and names) and return a GeoDataFrame                                                                           | `False`    |\n| names     | bool        | Add the unit ``name``                                                                                                                  | `False`    |\n| groups    |             | Coarser scales whose unit names to add as columns, e.g. ``[\"department\"]`` adds a ``department`` column (implies ``names``)            | `None`     |\n| ref       | str \\| None | Git branch, tag or commit to read from GitHub (default: local checkout or ``main``)                                                    | `None`     |\n\n## Notes {.doc-section .doc-section-notes}\n\nRaises ``ValueError`` for unknown variables, and for years that have no rows\n(listing the years the dataset has).\n\n## Example {.doc-section .doc-section-example}\n\n```python\n!pip install -q geo4bolivia\nimport geo4bolivia as geo\nimport plotly.express as px\n\ndf = geo.load(\"sdg05\", variables=[\"index_sdg5\"], years=[2012, 2024],\n              groups=[\"department\"])\npx.histogram(df, x=\"index_sdg5\", color=\"year\", barmode=\"overlay\",\n             labels=geo.labels(df), title=\"Gender equality index\")\n```\n\n\n::: {#707cefb8 .cell execution_count=1}\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:525px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/3.2.2/es5/tex-svg.min.js\"></script><script>if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-4.1.1.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-O24V1F27f8pb0glCkelh3cVHLNiHAJ5gCaVtq2aNch8=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"61b98c7f-74c6-4839-a21e-cb53a02bb4e2\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\"></div>            <script>                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                if (document.getElementById(\"61b98c7f-74c6-4839-a21e-cb53a02bb4e2\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"61b98c7f-74c6-4839-a21e-cb53a02bb4e2\",                    